depgraph: five resolver shortcuts recovered from the stage 3 runner-up, one new

Sub-series: N (stage 4, round 1) - patch 1 of 1; needs 0001-0030 (written on top of the full series).
Base: upstream 73646c35d.

The 30-patch ladder was cut from the winner of the last stage 3 round only; the
runner-up (r03-c1) held five changes that the winner did not, and they were lost.
An agent rebuilt them from the round diffs, ported them to 73646c35d and verified
them again; it added one change of its own (the last one below).
  * _slot_operator_update_probe: the _select_atoms_probe() test of an atom that
    ends its candidate loop without a candidate is put off and run only if it
    still matters (its author's estimate: 4.1 s of the six-state sum)
  * _pkgset_inert(): the --exclude / --useoldpkg-atoms / --reinstall-atoms sets
    are not asked about each package when they hold no atom at all (3.4 s)
  * _iter_atoms_for_pkg: argument atoms per (root, cp, package) are kept between
    calls; _set_args() clears the memo (2.3 s)
  * _iter_match_pkgs_any_newer goes through the cross-attempt match memo (1.5 s)
  * find_smallest_cycle: cheaper order of two comparisons in the leaf scan (0.2 s)
  * new: _iter_virt_update asked _virt_deps_visible() twice in a row for the same
    package; the second call is skipped when the first ran no package selection
    (2.2 s)
The per-change seconds are the author's split of the joint gain by instruction
counts, not separate wall measurements.

Judge, same load: 0001-0030 + C modules 99.5 s -> with this patch 90.1 s (-9.4 %);
unpatched 73646c35d 464.3 s.
Author's checks: 24 states equal to unpatched head (0-29 attempts, 0-2,578 packages,
six ending in a resolver error, 15 option combinations); a lock-step build ran old
and new code side by side: 96,223 skipped calls, 7.0 M empty-set and 2.6 M list
shortcuts, 1.23 M memo hits, 653,400 deferred probes, 690,423 memoised scans,
0 mismatches. Tester: 13 probes.
Weak spots named by the author: _pkgset_inert() reads internals of PackageSet;
the argument-atom memo relies on _set_args() being the only writer of the
argument atoms; the match memo is never trimmed.

Origin: written by AI agents (Claude) in stage 4 of the emerge-fast job, 2026-11-21, on
upstream commit 73646c35d with patches 0001-0030 and the C modules applied. Not a
human-written change. Judge: `emerge -p -uND @world` on six states of one system image, six
resolves in parallel, wall seconds summed; every run gave the same merge list in the same
order and the same number of backtracking attempts as unpatched 73646c35d. Black-box
testers (invented states, reference against candidate): 0 differences.

